Don't FATAL_ERROR when OpenVDB is absent

libslic3r already treats OpenVDB as optional via
    if (TARGET openvdb::openvdb)
in src/libslic3r/CMakeLists.txt:622-624. But the top-level
CMakeLists.txt aborted configure with FATAL_ERROR when the
bundled FindOpenVDB.cmake can't locate it.

Our Android build skips the OpenVDB-family deps (Blosc, IlmBase,
OpenEXR, OpenVDB) in patch 0001 — they don't cross-compile cleanly
and nothing in libslic3r's core mandates them. Downgrade the missing
OpenVDB message to STATUS so the configure continues. At runtime the
library is built without SLA hollowing / volumetric features that
use OpenVDB.

Retire-if: OpenVDB ever becomes mandatory in libslic3r, or we decide
to ship SLA volumetric support on Android.

---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 733d9a333f..0a794e1752 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -791,9 +791,13 @@ if(OpenVDB_FOUND)
     slic3r_remap_configs(IlmBase::Half RelWithDebInfo Release)
     slic3r_remap_configs(Blosc::blosc RelWithDebInfo Release)
 else ()
-    message(FATAL_ERROR "OpenVDB could not be found with the bundled find module. "
-                   "You can try to specify the find module location of your "
-                   "OpenVDB installation with the OPENVDB_FIND_MODULE_PATH cache variable.")
+    # OrcaXR: libslic3r already treats OpenVDB as optional
+    # (src/libslic3r/CMakeLists.txt:622-624 only links it `if (TARGET
+    # openvdb::openvdb)`). Downgrade this from FATAL_ERROR so Android
+    # builds (OpenVDB skipped in deps/) don't abort here. The SLA
+    # hollowing / volumetric features that use OpenVDB degrade rather
+    # than crash when the target is absent.
+    message(STATUS "OpenVDB not found — building without volumetric features.")
 endif ()
 
 find_path(SPNAV_INCLUDE_DIR spnav.h)
